  "narrative": {
    "intro": "Asrc Federal Facilities Logistics obligated $514M in FY2026 to date. Asrc Federal Facilities Logistics won 217,597 awards this period, with an average award size of $2.4K. Obligations fell 31.8% year over year. Asrc Federal Facilities Logistics has shifted its spending mix toward a few large market categories in FY2026 to date, led by Other Warehousing and Storage at $172M and Petroleum Lubricating Oil and Grease Manufacturing at $118M. Asrc Federal Facilities Logistics also recorded $61.2M in Adhesive Manufacturing and $59.4M in Electrical Apparatus and Equipment, Wiring Supplies, and Related Equipment Merchant Wholesalers. Past fiscal years show higher totals: FY21 was $549M, FY22 was $585M, FY23 was $714M, FY24 was $704M, and FY25 was $753M. Asrc Federal Facilities Logistics current-year totals are partial and represent fiscal year to date figures, not full-year totals. Use this snapshot to compare markets and award counts, and to spot concentration in warehousing and petroleum-related manufacturing for FY2026 to date.",
